IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er3-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), regulations 55.1 and 55.2: PROVISION OF INFORMATION by
-- employers, and RATIFICATION OF AMOUNTS PAID TO PERSONS WHILE NOT ENTITLED.
-- Written by the piece agent er3 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24 from the unofficial plain-text rendering
-- SOR-96-332.txt; nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- Out of range: s 10(2) of the Act as it read on October 25, 2009 (the benefit period that should have been
-- established; the old text is not among the inputs) and the programs of the Commission that verify claims. The
-- week's lying after the expiry of the benefit period that should have been established is an input.

§ `Regulation 55.1 -- provision of information`

-- The three items of information (a) to (c) that an employer who participates in the program provides about its
-- employees.
-- src:934 | (a) dates of commencement of employment;
-- src:935 | (b) periods of employment; and
-- src:936 | (c) amounts earned during employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55.1(a)-(c) (src:934-936)
DECLARE `er3 Item of information an employer provides` IS ONE OF
    `er3 information: dates of commencement of employment`     -- (a)
    `er3 information: periods of employment`                   -- (b)
    `er3 information: amounts earned during employment`        -- (c)

-- Employers who participate in a program to enable the Commission to substantiate the proof claimants give of
-- their fulfilment of the conditions for receiving or continuing to receive benefits "shall provide, electronically
-- on a monthly basis" the information in respect of their employees. The employer's duty is to the Commission; for
-- the person it means what is reported about them.
-- src:933 | 55.1 Employers who participate in a program to enable the Commission to substantiate proof provided to it by claimants in respect of their fulfilment of conditions for receiving or continuing to receive benefits shall provide, electronically on a monthly basis, the following information to the Commission in respect of their employees:
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55.1 (src:933)
GIVEN `the employer participates in a program to enable the Commission to substantiate proof provided to it by claimants in respect of their fulfilment of conditions for receiving or continuing to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 55.1 the employer must provide information about its employees electronically on a monthly basis` IF
    `the employer participates in a program to enable the Commission to substantiate proof provided to it by claimants in respect of their fulfilment of conditions for receiving or continuing to receive benefits`

-- src:933 | 55.1 Employers who participate in a program to enable the Commission to substantiate proof provided to it by claimants in respect of their fulfilment of conditions for receiving or continuing to receive benefits shall provide, electronically on a monthly basis, the following information to the Commission in respect of their employees:
-- src:934 | (a) dates of commencement of employment;
-- src:935 | (b) periods of employment; and
-- src:936 | (c) amounts earned during employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55.1 (src:933-936)
GIVEN `the employer participates in a program to enable the Commission to substantiate proof provided to it by claimants in respect of their fulfilment of conditions for receiving or continuing to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `er3 Item of information an employer provides`
DECIDE `reg 55.1 the information the employer provides about each employee each month` IS
    IF `reg 55.1 the employer must provide information about its employees electronically on a monthly basis` `the employer participates in a program to enable the Commission to substantiate proof provided to it by claimants in respect of their fulfilment of conditions for receiving or continuing to receive benefits`
    THEN LIST `er3 information: dates of commencement of employment`, `er3 information: periods of employment`, `er3 information: amounts earned during employment`
    ELSE EMPTY

§ `Regulation 55.2 -- ratification of amounts paid to persons while not entitled`

-- The Commission may ratify the amounts paid (a) to claimants whose benefit period was established from January 4,
-- 2009 to September 11, 2010 following a claim for special benefits; and (b) for a week after the expiry of the
-- benefit period that should have been established under s 10(2) of the Act as it read on October 25, 2009.
-- The "and" is read as joining the two: the amount is one paid to a claimant of kind (a) for a week of kind (b)
-- (fork F17). The Commission's power is not exercised here: the rule gives the conditions.
-- src:939 | 55.2 The Commission may ratify the amounts paid
-- src:940 | (a) to claimants whose benefit period was established in the period beginning on January 4, 2009 and ending on September 11, 2010 following a claim for special benefits; and
-- src:941 | (b) for a week that is after the expiry of the benefit period that should have been established with respect to them under subsection 10(2) of the Act, as it read on October 25, 2009.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55.2 (src:939-941)
GIVEN `the day on which the claimant's benefit period was established` IS A DATE
      `the benefit period was established following a claim for special benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the week is after the expiry of the benefit period that should have been established under subsection 10(2) of the Act, as it read on October 25, 2009` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 55.2 the amount paid for the week is one the Commission may ratify` IF
        `the day on which the claimant's benefit period was established` AT LEAST (YMD 2009 1 4)
    AND `the day on which the claimant's benefit period was established` AT MOST (YMD 2010 9 11)
    AND `the benefit period was established following a claim for special benefits`
    AND `the week is after the expiry of the benefit period that should have been established under subsection 10(2) of the Act, as it read on October 25, 2009`
